{"nodes": [{"id": "week_02_deal_risk_rubric_doc", "label": "Week 02 rubric: how the deal-risk answer key was written", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "week-02-deal-risk/rubric.md", "source_location": "L1-L9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "73 events across 20 open deals, every label by hand, against the same strings the models get, so disagreeing with a label means disagreeing with a visible rule that can be changed in src/ledger.py. Today is fixed at 2026-09-25 for the two rules that count days."}, {"id": "week_02_deal_risk_rubric_at_risk_answer_key", "label": "Answer key: eight at-risk deals ($1.145M of $2.79M)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "week-02-deal-risk/rubric.md", "source_location": "L106-L121", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ironbridge $240K competitor x2. Keystone $210K competitor x2. Datacore $185K no exec engagement in 30d. Halcyon $150K budget or timing slipped. Vantage $128K champion left. Cloudmark $94K 2 tickets escalated. Tidewater $76K budget or timing slipped. Precision $62K 3 tickets escalated and closes in 3d with open issues. The other twelve deals are healthy. ledger.py refuses to build unless the rule over the hand labels gives exactly this."}, {"id": "week_02_deal_risk_rubric_signal_traps", "label": "Signal edge-case traps (E036, E048, E044, E031, E073, E072)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-02-deal-risk/rubric.md", "source_location": "L38-L50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The traps sit on the edges between signals. A competitor named to be rejected (E036, Lumen Health) is momentum. Someone other than the champion leaving (E048, a support agent at Oakridge) is routine, because the champion is named on the deal record. A champion promoted inside the account (E044, Pinecrest) is momentum. How-to tickets (E031, E073) are routine. Layoffs where the team says the renewal is protected (E072, Driftwood) are stall at watch."}, {"id": "week_02_deal_risk_rubric_exec_window_events", "label": "exec_engaged 30-day window test events (E004 Datacore, E051 Summit Labs, E068 Silverline)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-02-deal-risk/rubric.md", "source_location": "L70-L80", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three events built around no_exec_30d. E004: Datacore's CTO is only cc'd, so the last real exec contact is the meeting 41 days earlier and the $185K deal is at risk. E051: a Summit Labs VP is cc'd but ran a meeting twelve days before, so the deal is fine. E068: the Silverline SVP sponsor call was 29 days before today, one day inside the window, on the biggest deal in the set."}, {"id": "week_02_deal_risk_rubric_label_distribution", "label": "Week 02 label distribution (73 events)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "week-02-deal-risk/rubric.md", "source_location": "L123-L132", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "signal: 32 momentum, 21 routine, 8 escalation, 5 competitor, 5 stall, 2 champion_exit. severity: 53 none, 6 watch, 13 serious, 1 critical (E033, Keystone choosing Corvid). exec_engaged: 17 true, 56 false. champion_exit has two examples, both on Vantage."}], "edges": [{"source": "week_02_deal_risk_src_spec_assess", "target": "week_02_deal_risk_readme_category_before_magnitude", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-02-deal-risk/rubric.md", "source_location": "L102-L104", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_02_deal_risk_rubric_at_risk_answer_key", "target": "week_02_deal_risk_src_ledger_label_rule_self_check", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-02-deal-risk/rubric.md", "source_location": "L119-L121", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_02_deal